'' FOR EACH CONVERTS each element to the LOOP VARIABLE's string kind, as fbc-modern does
'' (tiko-book T15). 'for each w as ustring' over a 'string' array initialised the ustring
'' with fb_StrInit -- narrow bytes in a UTF-16 descriptor, so "ab" read as one CJK unit and
'' three words hashed to three keys where fbc makes two. Run against fbc, the loops now
'' print the same text, lengths and code units, the iterator path included.
'' TEST: cli
'' ARGS: --dump-ir tests/mir/src/foreach-ustring-convert.bas
'' EXPECT-EXIT: 0
'' EXPECT-OUT: verify: ok
'' EXPECT-OUT: 0 statements not lowered
'' EXPECT-OUT: call.rtl ptr fb_UStrAssignFromA(@w, -1,
'' EXPECT-OUT: call.rtl ptr fb_UStrAssignToA(@t, -1,
'' EXPECT-OUT: call.rtl ptr fb_StrInit(@s, -1,
'' EXPECT-NOT: fb_StrInit(@w,
'' EXPECT-NOT: fb_UStrInit(@t,
